		<div class="post" id="post-1671013">
		<div class="long">
			<div class="head">
									<div class="options">
						<a href="javascript:;" onclick="togglePostFold(event,1671013)" class="btn btn-default btn-small btn-sm">Fold</a>
					</div>
								<div class="title" id="post-title-1671013">
																		
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/wishun" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1204404); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1204404&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608930948" alt="wishun" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1204404)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/wishun" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1204404); return false;" >wishun</a></span> <span class="odate time_1356556997 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">26 Dec 2012 21:23</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1671013">
									

<p>Okay, *deep breath* I am not trying to start another whole &quot;merits of AWCY?&quot; debate, and I fully support an author's right to define what a piece is or is not, but this screams AWCY? so hard that I have to question the adamant rejection.<br />
This story is, in theme, characters, and content, everything that defines the guerilla art GoI. If I had the skill (and inclination) to write &quot;the quintessential AAWCY? story&quot; it would come out manifestly equivalent to this tale.<br />
But the very first comment, taking priority over every other point of description or clarification, is an unequivical rejection of the very notion that this has any relation whatsoever.</p>
<p>I can conceive of only two scenarios, Gaffney. A) You have internalized the mind-set of AWCY? to a degree that I can hardly grasp, and have executed a meta-tale that went over all our heads. The equivalent of when Banksy tagged his own pieces &quot;This isn't art!&quot; B) You truly hate AWCY?, but you were writing, and this took shape, and it turned out too good to trash. So now you are in denial that you have furthered the existence of this GoI you hate.</p>
<p>tl;dr - I think this is AWCY?, because it fits too well not to be. But I feel bad for contradicting the author.</p>

							</div>

								
					
