    <div class="post-container" id="fpc-1671300">
                      
		<div class="post" id="post-1671300">
		<div class="long">
			<div class="head">
									<div class="options">
						<a href="javascript:;" onclick="togglePostFold(event,1671300)" class="btn btn-default btn-small btn-sm">Fold</a>
					</div>
								<div class="title" id="post-title-1671300">
																		SPOYLURZ SPELD OWT!!!!1
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser deleted" data-id="1324229"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/common--images/avatars/default/a16.png" alt=""/>(account deleted)</span> <span class="odate time_1356586863 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">27 Dec 2012 05:41</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1671300">
									

<p>In-universe, this has nothing to do with AWCY? and it bugs me that people keep insisting that does. Francis Lepage died over a decade before AWCY? came into existence, and he would probably have despised them if he ever met them. I was going to write a tale making Sarah Moutree a founding &quot;member&quot; of AWCY?/one of the creators of the original AWCY? &quot;joke,&quot; but am considering not writing it/writing with a different character out of spite. :P</p>
<p>Out-of-universe, this tale was an attempt to answer <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/forum/t-471950/why-i-think-awcy-doesn-t-suck#post-1470751">Digiwizzard's problem with AWCY?</a>, specifically,</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The thing is - and this is something that Swann touches upon in his 001 proposal - everyone on this site is ultimately an artist. We spend a lot of time dressing ourselves up in the trappings of rationalistic super sciency man, but in the end every SCP on this site is the culmination of the work of at least one, and sometimes multiple artists. I think there's something compelling about the fact that an artistic GOI would have to be a dark mirror of the writing base itself. We create horrible, terrifying and wonderful things for no real reason other then the feelings and thoughts that they engender in us.. And while I don't mean to literally make it some sort of meta self insert, it would create an uncomfortable situation where the created art (the Foundation) is in conflict with the artists themselves (us).</p>
<p>But what we have instead is &quot;What if Damien Hirst was a warlock?&quot;</p>
</blockquote>
<p>So yeah, it was an attempt to kind of have Lepage do the whole &quot;j'accuse&quot; thing, both in-universe and to the site as a whole.<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-46905-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-46905-1')">1</a></sup> If that was unclear, it was a failing on my part as a writer.</p>
<p>Or alternately, it's just a fun little story about an art student who has her life destroyed.</p>
<p>tl;dr Gaffney attempts to be clever, but only creates confusion.</p>
<div class="footnotes-footer">
<div class="title">Footnotes</div>
<div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-46905-1"><a href="javascript:;" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnoteref-46905-1')">1</a>. In-universe, he was doing in attempt to make &quot;better&quot; or &quot;stronger&quot; artists who would be conscious of their role, in contrast to the various artists who were creating the anomalous equivalent of Piss Christ, as a way of cementing his legacy</div>
</div>

							</div>

								
					
